From: hiliang <hiliang@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] whpx: expose APIC timer features the hypervisor emulates

WHvGetVirtualProcessorCpuidOutput hides CPUID.01H:ECX.TSC_DEADLINE_TIMER and
CPUID.06H:EAX.ARAT on hosts whose native CPUID layout differs (observed on an
AMD Ryzen 7 9700X host), even though the hypervisor's local-APIC emulation
accepts TSC-deadline MSR writes and QEMU's own LAPIC device implements the
same. Guests that probe these bits early (e.g. the x86_64 macOS kernel) then
select a timer mode different from the one QEMU actually emulates.

Force the two bits on the same way the function already forces X2APIC,
HYPERVISOR and HT: QEMU is the component that implements the behavior the
bits advertise, so reporting them is accurate regardless of the host CPUID
layout. This removes the "host doesn't support requested feature" warnings
for these bits under WHPX.

Signed-off-by: hiliang <hiliang@localhost>
---
 target/i386/whpx/whpx-all.c | 12 ++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+)

diff --git a/target/i386/whpx/whpx-all.c b/target/i386/whpx/whpx-all.c
index 0000000..0000001 100644
--- a/target/i386/whpx/whpx-all.c
+++ b/target/i386/whpx/whpx-all.c
@@ -1399,6 +1399,18 @@ uint32_t whpx_get_supported_cpuid(uint32_t func, uint32_t idx, int reg)
     if (func == 1) {
         ecx |= CPUID_EXT_X2APIC;
         ecx |= CPUID_EXT_HYPERVISOR;
+        /*
+         * Hyper-V's CPUID output hides the APIC timer modes on hosts whose
+         * native CPUID layout differs (e.g. AMD hosts), even though the
+         * hypervisor's local-APIC emulation handles TSC-deadline writes and
+         * the QEMU-side LAPIC device does the same for kernel-irqchip=off
+         * style operation. Guests that probe this bit early (e.g. the
+         * x86_64 macOS kernel) pick their timer based on it; exposing it
+         * matches what QEMU actually emulates, exactly like the X2APIC bit
+         * above.
+         */
+        ecx |= CPUID_EXT_TSC_DEADLINE_TIMER;
         edx |= CPUID_HT;
     }
+    if (func == 6) {
+        eax |= CPUID_6_EAX_ARAT;
+    }
 
     switch (reg) {
-- 
